Z||000007||Tigger||10-13-2000||09:20 AM||||Congrats on the new job!<P>I believe some if not all Saturn dealerships do a wash and detailing job on your Saturn every time you have it in for service.  It suprises many people when they go to pick up their car and it's squeeky klean.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">             <BR>    <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> <p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 10-13-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000008||william_thorniii||10-13-2000||10:08 AM||||Gt,<P>I detailed on and off professionally for about 6 years.  Usually as a 2nd job.  I loved it.  Towards the end, those nights of working being away from home from 7am-2am were killing me.  I worked both at dealerships and at an independant detailing shop.  If you have the right tools/chems it is a great job.  Otherwise you are always trying to conjure up something that is good enough.  <P>Good luck to you,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
